1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,700
Something smells good.

2
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:14,900
Hey, senshi?

3
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:22,640
There you are.

4
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:24,460
Oh, you're awake now.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Good morning to you.

6
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:28,040
I see you made breakfast.

7
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:29,560
Isn't it great?

8
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:31,640
Mr. Senshi's an amazing chef.

9
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:33,200
Yeah, you're right.

10
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,060
Senshi's the best there is.

11
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:43,580
Mmm.

12
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:46,440
Mmm, it's so tasty.

13
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:47,660
Yad.

14
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:48,100
Huh?

15
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:49,680
Do you want to try some, too?

16
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:52,700
But I won't be able to taste it.

17
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:53,680
Here.

18
00:00:53,680 --> 00:01:03,520
Oh, it's warm.

19
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:05,020
And it's soft as well.

20
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,580
Your sense of taste is almost like a muscle.

21
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:10,940
If you don't exercise it regularly, then it gets weak.

22
00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:14,800
So, start building it back up by enjoying textures first.

23
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:15,740
Got it.

24
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:16,720
Good.

25
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:17,740
Stay still.

26
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:26,900
A very long time ago, I used to dine with my parents and grandfather like this.

27
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:32,980
Always next to my grandfather was Thistle, who you may know as the Mad Mage.

28
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:37,620
My great-grandfather first brought him to the castle as a court jester.

29
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:40,880
I say that the two of them were raised like brothers.

30
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:47,600
Once my grandfather ascended the throne, Thistle was asked to learn magic and excelled in it.

31
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:55,240
These lands were originally filled with dwarven and elven artifacts, so there was likely black magic mixed in, too.

32
00:01:56,260 --> 00:02:02,240
Thistle soon became obsessed with power and eventually cast a spell of immortality on us.

33
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:05,320
Actually, we've been wanting to talk to him.

34
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:07,440
Do you know where he is right now?

35
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:08,660
Talk to him?

36
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:10,720
You're asking for the impossible.

37
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:13,780
A normal conversation is out of the question.

38
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:17,360
We went through great trouble to help my grandfather escape.

39
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:20,040
Those suspected of helping were executed.

40
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:27,660
But if you just want to meet him, the mage's eyes have started gathering because they've noticed a change here.

41
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:30,860
The Mad Mage himself will appear before long.

42
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:35,320
This dungeon is an extension of his arms and legs.

43
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:38,740
You are aware of his power, aren't you?

44
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:41,320
We are, but we still need to see him.

45
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:49,700
I don't know if you'll be able to talk, but go seek help from the winged lion that is imprisoned deep within the dungeon.

46
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:53,300
He might be able to subdue the mage's power.

47
00:02:53,300 --> 00:03:03,520
You can get inside the castle walls through here, meaning you'll be able to return to the dungeon.

48
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:05,700
Here you go. Take this with you.

49
00:03:06,020 --> 00:03:07,440
Thanks. You're too kind.

50
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:12,320
Let's not give them too much. It'll be a huge burden for those carrying them.

51
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:13,580
What does that mean?

52
00:03:13,980 --> 00:03:17,180
Simply that you'll be leaving this place the same way you came.

53
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:21,640
Thank you. All of you.

54
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:23,440
Good luck.

55
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:34,700
I know I shouldn't say this, but do you really think they're the chosen ones?

56
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,640
I truly wish to think so.

57
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:42,000
Hey, Yad.

58
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:43,800
Oh, Thistle.

59
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:47,640
Tell me, who were you just talking to?

60
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:55,240
Can we stop falling?

61
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:57,060
Wait, this is...

62
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:58,500
Ow, my back.

63
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:01,220
It's an ancient dwarven cistern.

64
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:04,620
So it's this whole place, huh? Which part of it are we in?

65
00:04:04,620 --> 00:04:07,080
My compass isn't working.

66
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:10,080
I guess I should have assumed this would happen, though.

67
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:11,440
Typical dwarves.

68
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:14,300
It looks like the remains of a defensive point.

69
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:15,680
Right?

70
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:19,280
Does he have traveling sickness?

71
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:23,300
Probably, since dwarves have sensitive semicircular canals.

72
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:25,340
Is it the same for gnomes as well?

73
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:28,120
That, on top of monosickness, I'd assume.

74
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:30,700
How'd we get here?

75
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:32,060
Oh, you're back?

76
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:33,980
Wait, what?

77
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:38,240
You okay?

78
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:40,460
Just rest here for a bit.

79
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:41,740
We're gonna take a look around.

80
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:46,160
Chill.

81
00:04:46,380 --> 00:04:46,520
Hmm?

82
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:48,940
You see these symbols on this pillar?

83
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,180
Oh, yeah.

84
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:53,500
I do see something.

85
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:56,780
Write down the symbols on the other pillars that are around us.

86
00:04:56,780 --> 00:04:59,420
I can tell roughly where we are that way.

87
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:01,340
How do you know a thing like that?

88
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:05,060
These types of places always have some kind of hidden code in them.

89
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:07,820
Well, I guess in this case,

90
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:11,640
it just goes to show that not all dwarves have a great sense of direction.

91
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:17,360
I know where we are.

92
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:20,000
Looks like we're somewhere in the southeastern part.

93
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:20,320
Hey!

94
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:22,240
Guys, we found something!

95
00:05:22,660 --> 00:05:23,940
Oh, that was fast.

96
00:05:23,940 --> 00:05:26,300
We might have found where Fallon is!

97
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:29,200
You're saying these are Fallon's tracks?

98
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,780
She noticed us getting closer and ran, but...

99
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:33,920
It was definitely her!

100
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:35,400
The silhouette said it all!

101
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:35,980
Right?

102
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:40,300
It seemed a lot closer to a griffin to me.

103
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:43,620
Remind me what a griffin is.

104
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:47,180
Its upper half's a bird, and its lower half is a lion.

105
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:50,480
There aren't records of this dungeon ever having a griffin.

106
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:53,020
Is this scent familiar?

107
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,540
They're not dogs, you know.

108
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:00,060
It reeks a beast.

109
00:06:00,620 --> 00:06:02,640
Either way, we need to catch up to it.

110
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:03,520
No, we don't.

111
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:04,940
Huh?

112
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:06,560
We don't?

113
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:07,240
But why?

114
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:09,480
Uh, well, it's just...

115
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:11,040
It might be Fallon, Senshi.

116
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:11,700
I...

117
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:12,460
Um...

118
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:13,460
Oh, over there.

119
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:15,580
I've never seen that kind of mushroom before.

120
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:16,620
Let's cook it.

121
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:17,660
Seriously?

122
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:20,120
They look vaguely familiar to me.

123
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:22,380
That said, I'm pretty sure they're poisonous,

124
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:23,420
so don't eat them.

125
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:25,580
I really don't like griffins.

126
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:28,660
Why are you so scared of a monster you've never even seen?

127
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,100
Whatever, let's just go!

128
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:30,740
No, please!

129
00:06:30,940 --> 00:06:31,440
Wait a minute!

130
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:33,760
It's too dangerous out here!

131
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:34,280
Move!

132
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:41,160
Whoa, I knew it!

133
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:42,600
A griffin!

134
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:48,280
How cool!

135
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:50,080
It's my first time seeing one!

136
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:51,500
A griffin?

137
00:06:52,260 --> 00:06:54,640
So I got all worked up for nothing?

138
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:57,080
Here it comes!

139
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:58,020
Leave it to me!

140
00:06:58,520 --> 00:06:59,000
Now!

141
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:11,020
It's too fast!

142
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:11,760
Senshi!

143
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:13,180
Don't run away with your back!

144
00:07:13,260 --> 00:07:13,760
Turn to it!

145
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:22,580
Senshi!

146
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:22,860
Senshi!

147
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:32,620
Oh, no.

148
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:35,820
It happened so fast.

149
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:36,660
I was useless.

150
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:39,120
Did anyone see if he had a weapon on him?

151
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,600
He didn't have one.

152
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:42,040
We have to go find him.

153
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:45,200
Maybe someone should climb on top of each pillar to look?

154
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:46,860
He ain't gonna be me, though.

155
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:48,400
Which way did they go?

156
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:51,000
We can't do anything if they're somewhere up high.

157
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,720
We won't even find his corpse.

158
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:55,060
He has no way to defend himself.

159
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:57,480
Are we really never gonna see him again?

160
00:07:58,340 --> 00:07:58,740
Marcel!

161
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:00,300
How do we save Senshi?

162
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:06,700
I'll use a familiar to find him!

163
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:09,680
You're going to summon a monster?

164
00:08:10,340 --> 00:08:13,420
It's not so much summoning one as it is creating one.

165
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:15,620
There are three types of summoning.

166
00:08:16,060 --> 00:08:19,220
One, taking control of existing spirits or monsters.

167
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:21,700
The conditions for it are complicated,

168
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:24,220
and it's likely the Lord of the Dungeon will notice.

169
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,040
Two, turning plants or animals into monsters.

170
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:32,080
This one also isn't ideal because you need a lot of prep time.

171
00:08:32,760 --> 00:08:34,740
Three, making them yourself.

172
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:36,320
That's what I'll be doing.

173
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:38,300
That one sounds the most difficult.

174
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:41,540
It is if you're trying to make a fully independent creature,

175
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:44,900
but for now, we just need it to be able to move at least.

176
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:48,260
While I prep the magic circle,

177
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:50,620
can you gather all the meat we have in the pan?

178
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:51,400
Sure thing.

179
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:56,920
That's everything?

180
00:08:57,420 --> 00:08:59,400
It'd be nice if you could find a bit more.

181
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:03,040
There, that's it.

182
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:05,620
Although we do have some cheese and eggs...

183
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:06,280
Veggies, too!

184
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,900
Guess it'd still add to the calories.

185
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:11,180
Bring them!

186
00:09:11,540 --> 00:09:11,820
Right!

187
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:18,360
What monster are you making?

188
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:20,100
Is it gonna obey you?

189
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:21,820
Could you teach me how to...

190
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:22,040
No!

191
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:25,720
Go and get yourself certified to handle dangerous magic first!

192
00:09:27,420 --> 00:09:29,020
Wait, is that really a thing?

193
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:32,800
So, who exactly is that old dwarf guy anyway?

194
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:35,540
How'd he end up in your party in the first place?

195
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:37,800
And why is he so obsessed with making food?

196
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:39,800
Huh?

197
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:42,840
How do you not know the answer to that?

198
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:44,580
You all act like you're old buddies!

199
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:47,740
I mean, I suppose we've never had a chance to ask.

200
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:50,980
I can relate not wanting to discuss personal matters with people.

201
00:09:52,060 --> 00:09:55,340
Although, I'd be lying if I said I wasn't curious.

202
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:58,220
There are several things that I'm still hung up on.

203
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:01,560
Do you remember what he said to us back when we first met him?

204
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:06,260
It's been a decade since he started researching monster food in this dungeon.

205
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:09,620
But this dungeon was only discovered six years ago.

206
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:10,840
That's true.

207
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:15,600
Also, every single piece of cookware he uses is made from high-quality metal.

208
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:18,560
He was able to decipher ancient dwarven codes.

209
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:21,500
He's afraid of a monster from a floor we just reached.

210
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:23,920
And he always treats me like a child.

211
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:26,120
Isn't that last one a misunderstanding?

212
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:27,140
No.

213
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:30,480
People who don't know about our kind usually jump to that conclusion.

214
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:33,220
They don't realize that half-foots are another race.

215
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:36,900
So they assume that we become a tall man or a dwarf when we get older.

216
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:41,740
However, that only comes from a few regions like the East.

217
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:45,060
If he's lived here ten years, there's no reason he shouldn't know.

218
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:49,460
Could it be that Senshi isn't from the surface?

219
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:55,200
Some time after we rescue him, why don't we ask him to reintroduce himself to us?

220
00:10:58,460 --> 00:10:58,940
Huh?

221
00:10:58,940 --> 00:11:21,020
Is it over now?

222
00:11:21,020 --> 00:11:23,040
It should be.

223
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:25,440
Let's try to open the lid.

224
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:45,040
Oh, thank goodness.

225
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:47,460
I was almost worried I wouldn't succeed.

226
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:48,980
What's that face?

227
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:50,780
I said they just needed to move, right?

228
00:11:50,860 --> 00:11:53,880
I couldn't spare the resources to make them aesthetically pleasing, okay?

229
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:55,120
Now go.

230
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:58,840
What's wrong?

231
00:11:59,740 --> 00:12:03,440
Its vision is overlapping with my own, and it feels awful.

232
00:12:03,860 --> 00:12:05,540
Can someone put a blindfold on me?

233
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:12,920
How can the mad mage send out so many of these things and also process their info all at once?

234
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:13,680
I'm curious.

235
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:15,820
You can think about that stuff later.

236
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:16,780
Senshi first.

237
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:21,300
I'll look for abnormalities based on the dungeon cleaners and spirits around here.

238
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:22,820
Follow my familiar.

239
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:25,800
Huh?

240
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:28,580
Are you not going to be able to keep up?

241
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:31,180
Do you know how hard it is to walk while flying?

242
00:12:31,660 --> 00:12:32,780
I'm going to carry her.

243
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:34,920
Would you two mind carrying our bags?

244
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,140
And here we go.

245
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:39,400
Wait, I'm scared.

246
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:41,220
Grab around here.

247
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:41,720
No way!

248
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:43,160
Are you trying to make me fall?

249
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:44,380
Stop moving so much!

250
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:49,400
What the hell is she doing with her arms?

251
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:51,860
I guess this is what makes her feel safe.

252
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:00,260
That pillar!

253
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:02,600
The dungeon cleaners are flocking to it!

254
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:03,520
That's the place!

255
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:06,800
Senshi!

256
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:07,900
There!

257
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:08,560
Found him!

258
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:10,740
The griffon trapped him on a pillar up ahead!

259
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:11,540
I see.

260
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:12,860
Griffons do that?

261
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:14,700
We're here to save you, Senshi!

262
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:15,900
Can you tell it's me?

263
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:16,840
A fly?

264
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:21,480
Crap!

265
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:23,180
How do I get him down?

266
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:24,700
Just be careful, Marcel.

267
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:27,080
Griffons have exceptional vision.

268
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:31,620
It'll already be watching you before you even notice it.

269
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:36,380
I lost my eyes up there.

270
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:39,500
Griffons' bodies are very functional.

271
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:41,460
Their wings are powerful,

272
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:44,300
and their graceful bodies allow them to adapt quickly.

273
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:46,860
Plus, their sharp beak and claws,

274
00:13:47,180 --> 00:13:48,560
they're near impossible to avoid.

275
00:13:49,460 --> 00:13:51,720
Creatures are the way they look because of necessity.

276
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:54,520
They have no need to just be aesthetically pleasing.

277
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:55,760
Hmm.

278
00:13:56,180 --> 00:13:56,900
Fine, then.

279
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:59,680
What shape should it take to match up to a griffon?

280
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:01,560
Hmm.

281
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:06,140
You sure that horn is necessary?

282
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:08,660
This shape will make it a lot more aerodynamic.

283
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:11,440
So now it'll be able to move much quicker.

284
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:15,100
Do you remember the wyverns that the mad mage had patrolling?

285
00:14:15,780 --> 00:14:17,420
They were as fast as an arrow.

286
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:19,700
Let's try to aim for that shape.

287
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:25,420
Send it out like this and see the difference it makes.

288
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:31,600
It moves so fast now!

289
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:33,000
I think this'll work!

290
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:35,080
Until Senshi's back on the ground,

291
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:36,960
I'll try to distract the griffon!

292
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:39,440
Everyone else cover me and prepare for battle!

293
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:41,640
Why is she flapping?

294
00:14:42,020 --> 00:14:44,060
Maybe it gives her a sense of unity.

295
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:46,300
All right, Senshi.

296
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:47,960
Grab onto this rope!

297
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:51,200
Now, the next move is...

298
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,960
So fast!

299
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:55,640
I have to lead it away!

300
00:14:56,040 --> 00:14:56,700
Come on!

301
00:14:56,760 --> 00:14:57,460
Over here!

302
00:15:01,980 --> 00:15:04,060
Just get to the ground and...

303
00:15:06,140 --> 00:15:11,400
It got me again.

304
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,520
This is bad.

305
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:15,280
I can't even compete with it.

306
00:15:15,660 --> 00:15:16,440
What do I do?

307
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:18,440
You can leave everything to me!

308
00:15:18,680 --> 00:15:19,460
I've got this!

309
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:20,700
I'll make it way stronger!

310
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,380
I'll put more horns here,

311
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:23,300
arrange the fangs,

312
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:24,500
equip it with sharp claws,

313
00:15:24,620 --> 00:15:25,280
add some scales,

314
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:26,160
and...

315
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:27,140
Give it two heads!

316
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:29,380
Now all of its strength and abilities are doubled!

317
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:31,140
It breathes fire and ice!

318
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:31,920
So cool!

319
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:34,680
How can it win a fight against a griffon?

320
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:36,320
Does it need more attack?

321
00:15:36,620 --> 00:15:37,400
Or more defense?

322
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:38,540
No!

323
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:38,600
No!

324
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:45,700
It doesn't need claws or fangs!

325
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:45,780
It doesn't need claws or fangs!

326
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,900
Something fast, elegant, and beautiful!

327
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:52,600
What I need is the resolution and ego

328
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:55,800
to create a creature made solely to save Senshi!

329
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:57,700
It was in that moment

330
00:15:57,700 --> 00:15:59,780
that all of Marcil's thoughts

331
00:15:59,780 --> 00:16:01,260
and her prayers

332
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:03,560
manifested into a miracle.

333
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:06,080
I shall bestow you with a name!

334
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:08,780
Silver wings that will soar the heavens!

335
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:12,060
I summon thee...

336
00:16:12,060 --> 00:16:13,000
Skyfish!

337
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:14,660
So...

338
00:16:14,660 --> 00:16:15,720
stupid.

339
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:16,780
Shut up!

340
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:17,480
It's fine!

341
00:16:17,980 --> 00:16:18,800
Now then,

342
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:19,740
time to fly!

343
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:27,580
So fast!

344
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:28,780
You move so creepily!

345
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:30,400
I'm going all out!

346
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:32,000
Everyone, prepare for battle!

347
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,460
What the hell is she doing now?

348
00:16:34,640 --> 00:16:35,320
Her best!

349
00:16:35,740 --> 00:16:36,920
Or something close.

350
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:41,320
Yeah!

351
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:45,260
Whoa!

352
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:47,200
It's hard to control this thing!

353
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:51,260
All right!

354
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:53,320
Now this time...

355
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:56,380
I'll turn around and...

356
00:16:56,380 --> 00:16:57,400
pierce through!

357
00:16:57,400 --> 00:17:22,840
Are you hurt?

358
00:17:23,260 --> 00:17:24,080
I'm fine.

359
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:26,540
We should probably take a good rest.

360
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:28,700
You go relax over there, Senshi.

361
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:29,760
While I do the cooking.

362
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:30,100
Huh?

363
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:31,900
Huh?

364
00:17:38,740 --> 00:17:39,720
Thank you.

365
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:42,460
Rest in peace,

366
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:44,460
my Skyfish.

367
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:47,900
Whoa!

368
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:50,280
This is actually pretty cool.

369
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:52,740
Vegetables are packed in there like organs.

370
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:56,960
Did you need it for something?

371
00:17:57,460 --> 00:17:59,820
No, not really, but...

372
00:17:59,820 --> 00:18:00,940
I just, you know,

373
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:03,680
was hoping to have a little more time to mourn,

374
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:04,840
and now I can't.

375
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:06,400
Are you okay, Senshi?

376
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,400
I don't know.

377
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:07,900
I don't know.

378
00:18:07,900 --> 00:18:08,400
I don't know.

379
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:08,820
I don't know.

380
00:18:08,820 --> 00:18:09,400
I don't know.

381
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:10,040
I don't know.

382
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:10,820
I don't know.

383
00:18:10,820 --> 00:18:11,180
I don't know.

384
00:18:11,180 --> 00:18:11,760
I don't know.

385
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:12,720
I don't know.

386
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:16,420
It's fine.

387
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:17,540
Do whatever.

388
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:21,700
Chop up the summon creature into the desired length.

389
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:23,820
Trim off the wings at the base.

390
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:27,680
Squeeze out all the moisture with a scrap of cloth.

391
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:29,380
Salt and pepper.

392
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,620
Take the wings and roll them.

393
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:34,540
Dunk each piece of meat you chopped earlier

394
00:18:34,540 --> 00:18:36,740
into a mixture of flour, egg, and water.

395
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,100
Then fry.

396
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:40,420
For the wings,

397
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:42,480
quickly dip them in oil to cook them.

398
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:44,120
Serve with a sauce,

399
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:46,200
and it's ready.

400
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:58,000
This is seriously the perfect fusion of meat and veggies.

401
00:18:58,480 --> 00:18:59,540
If you say so.

402
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:03,360
You think summoning spells could play a big part in the art of cooking?

403
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:04,600
I sure hope not,

404
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:07,380
considering you need to sacrifice a week's worth of ingredients.

405
00:19:08,420 --> 00:19:08,940
Damn it.

406
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:11,100
I knew I should have brought some of that ale with me.

407
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:13,840
Make sure you eat more than just the wings, Izutsumi.

408
00:19:14,420 --> 00:19:14,900
Nuh-uh.

409
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:17,360
Have a bite, Senshi.

410
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:19,740
Worried about the griffon?

411
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:22,020
We're draining its blood help?

412
00:19:22,480 --> 00:19:22,920
Maybe.

413
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:25,700
No, that's not it.

414
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:28,720
I-I'm just not all that hungry at the moment.

415
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:33,300
Hey, uh, Senshi.

416
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:37,620
My name is Chilchuk.

417
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,940
I was born in a small village

418
00:19:39,940 --> 00:19:41,780
found in a basin to the northeast.

419
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:44,880
Since about ten years ago,

420
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:47,260
I've been doing odd jobs in various dungeons.

421
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:49,460
Piclocking, translation,

422
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:50,900
even being the middleman.

423
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:52,380
Also,

424
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:54,500
I have a wife and kids,

425
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:56,600
but for reasons I haven't seen them in a while.

426
00:19:57,120 --> 00:19:57,520
Uh!

427
00:19:58,340 --> 00:19:58,960
A wife and kids?

428
00:19:58,960 --> 00:20:01,040
Well, that about sums it up for my backstory.

429
00:20:01,820 --> 00:20:03,880
You mind telling us some stuff about you?

430
00:20:04,960 --> 00:20:06,800
How'd you end up living in this dungeon?

431
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:08,580
Did something happen?

432
00:20:11,540 --> 00:20:11,980
Hmm.

433
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:17,400
My name is Senshi of Izganda.

434
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:21,240
I used to be a member of a small mining group.

435
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:24,560
And while I say a mining group,

436
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:26,620
we weren't actually looking to collect ore.

437
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:28,680
What we were really after

438
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:30,580
were ruins that stood before the war,

439
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:32,120
hoping to strike it rich.

440
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:35,900
But ore is most of what we dug up each day, of course.

441
00:20:36,600 --> 00:20:37,520
If we were lucky,

442
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,120
we would come across a few relics

443
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:40,620
like cogwheels and lenses

444
00:20:40,620 --> 00:20:42,120
every once in a while.

445
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,120
Then one day,

446
00:20:44,260 --> 00:20:45,440
after some usual digging,

447
00:20:45,920 --> 00:20:48,100
we dug our way to something huge.

448
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:49,220
Oh.

449
00:20:49,220 --> 00:20:52,260
An ancient castle,

450
00:20:52,700 --> 00:20:54,420
brilliantly shining with gold.

451
00:20:55,660 --> 00:20:56,340
That's right.

452
00:20:57,020 --> 00:20:58,600
It was this very dungeon.

